 and 18.2 cm in length. One of the nests had nine cells, six of which were parasitized by Xystromutilla (five males and one female emerged) and two by Photocryptus sp. (Ichneumonidae: Cryptinae). The other two parasitized nests contained one cell each, from which emerged a male and a female. Therefore, six males and two females emerged in total from the nests. The males were larger bodied with average head width 0.3 mm (n = 6; SD = 0.01 mm) and the females 0.2 mm (n = 2; SD = 0.06 mm). We found in Xystromutilla bucki that the average time between nest collection and adult wasp emergence, for seven of the eight specimens reared, was 265 days (n = 7; SD = 4.2 days), with immatures exhibiting diapause at the prepupal stage (6 males, 1 female). Only one female (from the one-celled nest) did not enter into diapause, but rather emerged 11 days after nest collection.","","text","",""]]},"TZTBG":{"d":[["Distribution. China (Shaanxi).","","text","",""]]},"V6ZZK":{"d":[["Middle America","","text","",""]]},"V97XM":{"d":[["Oklahoma","48387","mrgid","",""]]},"VBYXB":{"d":[["Colombia","","text","",""]]},"VC97B":{"d":[["Bangladesh","","text","",""]]},"W9YB":{"d":[["Australia","","text","native",""]]},"WLS5":{"d":[["","ER","iso","",""],["","KE","iso","",""],["","UG","iso","",""],["","ZA","iso","",""]]},"Y7WD":{"d":[["Madagascan(Madagascar)","","text","",""]]},"Y86D":{"d":[["Rep. South Africa","","text","native",""]]},"YFXT":{"d":[["NWGPN","","text","native",""]]},"YFY3":{"d":[["","PER-OO","tdwg","native",""],["Peru","","text","native",""]]},"YG7T":{"d":[["MDG","MDG","tdwg","",""]]},"Z4ZC":{"d":[["Argentina (Catamarca, Jujuy, La Rioja, Salta, Tucuman)","","text","",""]]},"Z59C":{"d":[["Colombian Exclusive Economic Zone","8426","mrgid","",""]]}}